                <td width=572 valign=center colspan=10 style="width:343.6000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:none;
mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">This course focuses on drug-induced kidney injury, encompassing common nephrotoxic agents such as antimicrobials, antineoplastic drugs, and antipyretic analgesics and anti-inflammatory drugs. It systematically explains drug-related glomerular diseases, tubulointerstitial disorders, and vascular diseases, with in-depth exploration of their pathogenesis, histopathological alterations, and clinical manifestations. By integrating perspectives from pharmacology, pathophysiology, pathology, and clinical medicine—supplemented with case study analyses—the curriculum equips students with diagnostic and preventive competencies for medication-related renal injury, laying a robust foundation for safe medication practices in future clinical settings.</span></p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="height:19.9000pt;">
                <td width=777 valign=center colspan=14 style="width:466.7000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
